nal page of contributor \"${name}\" with information about their contributions to the project.`",{"type":23,"value":119},"Contribution",{"type":23,"value":97},{"type":23,"value":122},"Key elements",{"type":23,"value":124},"Connections",{"type":23,"value":126},"Begin Learning!",{"type":23,"value":128},"This material is for learners with a high level of knowledge. It contains information that is not suitable for beginners!",{"type":23,"value":130},"Need to know",{"type":23,"value":95},{"type":23,"value":133},"Depends on",{"type":23,"value":135},"This material is in development! It may change in the future and even contain errors!",{"type":23,"value":137},"Used by",{"type":23,"value":99},{"type":23,"value":140},"Externals",{"type":23,"value":142},"This is an optional material is for learners who want to dive deeper and gain additional knowledge and context.",{"type":28,"value":144},"(contentTitle) => `Clear and interesting explanation of the topic \"${contentTitle}\". Clear examples, important terms and statements, interesting facts, life applications.`",{"type":28,"value":146},"(contentTitle) => `Summary of the topic \"${contentTitle}\": key definitions, theorems, properties and examples of their use. All the most important things in a concise form!`",{"type":28,"value":148},"(contentTitle) => `Various problems with hints and answers on the topic \"${contentTitle}\". Interesting conditions, hints and detailed solutions. Turn knowledge into a skill!`",{"m":150},"function m(number, one, few, includeNumber = true) {\n  const text = number === 1 ? one : few;\n  return includeNumber ? `${number} ${text}` : text;\n}",{"contentPath":152,"mainContent":153},"page/faq/",{"fullId":9,"shortId":9,"contentRelativePath":154,"title":10,"breadcrumbs":155,"description":156,"flags":157,"stats":158,"contributions":161,"type":8,"proseElement":167,"storage":221,"toc":227},"00-faq",[],"\n    Answers to frequently asked questions: what is this site? why is it needed? who is it for?\n    Recommendations for effectively using the site's features to learn mathematics.\n    If you've just arrived at this site, start here.\n  ",{"dev":12},{"elements":159},{"accent_important":160},1,[162],{"contributorId":163,"name":164,"avatarUrl":165,"description":166},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","/file/contributors/gwynerva/avatar.png","Idea and main content.",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":168,"children":169},"mix",[170,175,182,188],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":171,"data":172,"id":174},"heading",{"level":160,"title":173},"The Role of \"Foundations\"","the-role-of-foundations",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":176,"children":177,"id":181},"paragraph",[178],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":180},"text","A starting point for everyone who doesn't have a clue about math at all. Doesn't know how to work with fractions, doesn't know how to solve equations or why they are needed, gets stuck on roots and powers, or for whom the concept of \"irrational number\" sounds like something from a sci-fi movie, and so on. If any of this (or all of it) describes you, start here:","paragraph-WnuowcFxPQm2",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":183,"data":184,"storageKey":186,"id":187},"referenceBlock",{"label":185},"All the most basic, simple, and necessary stuff. Absolutely all other materials on \"Open Math\" are written with the expectation that you have firmly grasped these foundations.","\u003Clink:global>/foundations","referenceBlock-a3ceWGgysyFf",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":189,"data":190,"children":193,"id":220},"accent_important",{"title":191,"layout":192},"No links to foundations!","column",[194],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":195,"children":196},"accentMain_important",[197],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":176,"children":198,"id":219},[199,201,209,211,217],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":200},"In most materials on this site ",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":202,"data":203,"children":205,"id":208},"emphasis",{"type":204,"accent":12},"bold",[206],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":207},"you won't find links","emphasis-vah5OoqzhXqb",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":210}," to definitions, theorems, and formulas from the \"Math Foundations\" book. ",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":202,"data":212,"children":213,"id":216},{"type":204,"accent":12},[214],{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":215},"This is not a mistake!","emphasis-HmK6rSdwK1ks",{"__JSPROSE_element":12,"schemaName":179,"data":218}," These are considered basics that every reader must know, understand, and be able to use \"by default\". This way, we don't clutter the text with endless links to elementary stuff.","paragraph-rj8F9p7w4YFt","no-links-to-foundations",{"\u003Clink:global>/foundations":222},{"type":223,"content":224,"resolvedHref":18,"previewRequest":225},"contentItem",{"contentType":15,"contentTitle":16},{"type":226,"contentType":15,"fullId":5},"content-page",[228],{"type":171,"level":160,"title":173,"elementId":174,"children":229},[],{"contributorsCount":160,"sponsorsCount":231},0,{"cameo":233},[234,235,236,237,238,239,240,241,242],"cameo-black-hole","cameo-confucius","cameo-dunno","cameo-einstein","cameo-euclid","cameo-gagarin","cameo-gauss","cameo-newton","cameo-t800",1770360369172]